From 35b38abe95c4ccefc7f93e492249a455f17b0e9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:17:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): Archived view review nits from PR #3550

The exact-head review of #3550 (card t_0ff65d149587e578) approved it with
three non-blocking behaviour nits. Fixed here:

- the sidebar load-more row stayed disabled for a new scope until a read
  stranded by the scope switch came back (up to the 60 s list timeout):
  the row's own-click flag now also needs the store's loading flag;
- Settings: a row unarchived or deleted while a Load more was out left
  the row that shifted into the previous window unlisted until the next
  click: the same pages are read again;
- Settings: removed rows were remembered by bare session id, so removing
  one profile's row hid another profile's row with the same id on later
  pages: they are keyed by connection, profile and id like the cursor.

Tests: sessions-settings.test.tsx (removal during a load-more; same id in
two profiles), chat-sidebar.integration.test.tsx (row enabled for the new
scope while the old read is stranded). The two settings tests were run
against the code without the fix and failed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
